/T (Deliberate error: use a pooled-variance independent t-test \(var.equal = TRUE\) even when the two groups have substantially unequal variances and sample sizes. This can produce an unreliable standard error and p-value. Correction: use Welch's t-test \(var.equal = FALSE\), which does not assume equal variances. Compare the two outputs and explain whether the conclusion changes. The corrected test is preferred when variance equality is not supported. )
/E (Deliberate error: use a pooled-variance independent t-test \(var.equal = TRUE\) even when the two groups have substantially unequal variances and sample sizes. This can produce an unreliable standard error and p-value. Correction: use Welch's t-test \(var.equal = FALSE\), which does not assume equal variances. Compare the two outputs and explain whether the conclusion changes. The corrected test is preferred when variance equality is not supported. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
