<<
/Title (TheNSL-KDDdataset is abenchmark and may not represent current production networks. Class imbalance, duplicated or correlated connection patterns, historical attack signatures and missing contextual variables can limit generalisation. A significant association between protocol and class is not proof that the protocol causes an attack. A statistically significant byte or duration difference may still be too small to justify a blocking rule. Security teams should validate promising findings on current, independently collected network traffic before changing controls.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1023 0 R
/First 1083 0 R
/Last 1083 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
